A||||20||AkursedX||Got in my 1st accident today||||9||
Z||000000||AkursedX||11-20-2001||09:58 PM||||Well there goes my unblemished driving record of 5 years....<P>I was at a stoplight and the light turned green and we all started moving and the guy 2 cars in front of me stops suddenly to turn, the guy in front of me slams on his brakes, I slam on mine, lock my tires (wet pavement) and slam into his rear end!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>The good news is that no damage was done to his car, so he let me go without having to do the whole insurance thing.  My car on the otherhand got the worst of it.  <BR> My front fascia is all scratched and has a bunch of spiderwebbing (I just repainted it 2 months ago) and my front decklid got jammed foward about an inch on the passenger side. My frontend slid underneath his car (chevy lumina)  <BR>So I went home, and took my decklid off and I had to bend the hinge back into place, and I managed to get a majority of the scratches out, but it still looks crappy up close.<P>But I guess it could of been worse.  The decklid is fine, and I can repaint the fascia in spring for free since I still have paint leftover.<P>BTW this is my 87GT, my 88GT is still flawless and sleeping for the winter  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I would of probably cried if it was that car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||RadRuss||11-20-2001||10:28 PM||||dude that sux!! i know how u feel cause these buffaloneons cant drive worth a $H!t. i am glad that it wasnt ur 88, and the dude let u off. best of luck, as for me i have to take the people who hit me to court inorder to get my money <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_14.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||banditbalz||11-20-2001||10:34 PM||||Joe, good to hear nobody was hurt. I have problems with my fronts locking up under panic situations as well. Have had a few close calls myself. You have any pics of your '87?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jake_2m4||11-20-2001||11:12 PM||||I was going to sad if it was your 88.  But it still sucks, glad to hear it wasn't worse.<P>Jake||||reg||1
Z||000004||AkursedX||11-21-2001||12:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by banditbalz:<BR><B>Joe, good to hear nobody was hurt. I have problems with my fronts locking up under panic situations as well. Have had a few close calls myself. You have any pics of your '87?<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>It didn't help that I'm driving on 195-75-14 winter tires.  They don't exactly provide the best grip.  <BR>As for the pics, I will probably snap some of the damage tomorrow, or thursday.  I will post a pic of what the car looked like before all the work tomorrow though.  But I won't have any good pics for a couple weeks.  That's when I'll have the time to finish stripping the GT rims and then they will be painted all black and have Dunlop 205/60-15's mounted on them.  <P>If I didn't do my own painting, I probably would be pissed about this.  Because this car is pretty nice.  New brakes, KYB shocks, all new ball joints and some new bushings, only 83k on the engine and burns no oil but the oil pressure is too low for my liking.  All the underbody has been sandblasted and repainted. All it needs is a new cat and muffler, front speakers, EGR valve and an O2 sensor and the car will be in great condition. The car is pretty clean, but in comparison to my 88, it's just not the same.  <BR>||||reg||1
