Z||000009||grinthock||11-21-2001||07:54 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>Rear ending someone is almost always totally your fault, your supposed to leave a lot of stopping distance, especially on wet pavement with fiero brakes.  Tough break man, but it sounds like you got off easy.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not trying to start a flame session dude, but why the hell is it when someone is down on their luck you just start kicking them.<P>YEAH HE KNOWS IT IS HIS FAULT TECHNICALLY.<P>But when someone slams on your brakes and didn't signal, give me a brake, that's unfair, Yeah your fault but still.<P>Leave people alone, comments like yours are not necessary.  Many people here were starting to like you, don't blow it now.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fformula88||11-21-2001||10:27 AM||||That really stinks, but luckily your 88 was spared!  I nailed a green Taurus wagon last winter on the 33.  It passed me in the left hand lane (I was driving my fathers 87 coupe) when it laid on its brakes to prevent hitting the car in front of him, spun sideways right into my lane.  I hit the brakes but was doing probably 40-45 when I nailed it.  The Taurus was literally turned into a horseshoe!  The 87 coupe suffered the front end getting pushed in a little, cracked the right fender, broke a headlight mounting point (they were up thankfulle, or they would have been crushed) and made the whole car about an inch short!  Radiator was fine. <P>After I got home and took it apart, I saw the energy absorber had gone under the Taurus and the impact bar took the brunt of the collision.  The ends of the frame rails were aslo pinched in about an inch.  But now the car is rebuilt.  We stripped a junked 87, my uncle got the frame pulled out a bit and we re-assembled it.  The final product came out good, with only a slightly wide gap between the hood and front fascia.<P>I must say, I am very impressed with how well the Fiero handles a good front end collision!  Good luck with your repairs!!<P>||||reg||1
