Z||000012||AkursedX||11-21-2001||12:43 PM||||Yeah I'm more than sure it would of been my fault.  I was so close because this happened just after the light, and I was just starting to give myself distance on the other guy. I don't even think I was above 20mph yet.  I probably hit the guy at around 5-10mph. <P> I guess I'm just used to being able to stop better because my 88 stops so well, even it wet pavement.  But the tires I have on the 87 basically suck on anything but snow.<P>Technically it doesn't ruin my perfect driving record because I didn't have to let the insurance company know about it, but it ruins it in my mind.  And I really took alot of pride in that.  Oh well I guess.    ||||reg||1
